     2	## Changelog
     3	
     4	Refer to the [2.14 Upgrade Guide](https://docs.nats.io/release-notes/whats_new/whats_new_214) for backwards compatibility notes with 2.12.x. Please note that the 2.13.x version was skipped.
     5	
     6	### Go Version
     7	
     8	- 1.26.4 (#8281)
     9	
    10	### Dependencies
    11	
    12	- golang.org/x/crypto v0.53.0 (#8297)
    13	- golang.org/x/sys v0.46.0 (#8297)
    14	- github.com/nats-io/jwt/v2 v2.8.2
    15	- github.com/nats-io/nkeys v0.4.16
    16	
    17	### Improved
    18	
    19	General
    20	
    21	- Per-connection log lines that could be noisy in normal operation have been demoted to debug level (#8289)
    22	- Writer options are now applied consistently when using the `s2_fast` compression mode (#8047)
    23	
    24	JetStream
    25	
    26	- Stream and consumer assignment handling has been refactored for more consistent migration and info behavior (#8262)
    27	- Meta, stream and consumer write errors are now registered more consistently for health and recovery handling (#8293)
    28	
    29	### Removed
    30	
    31	Monitoring
    32	
    33	- JSONP callback support has been removed from monitoring endpoints
    34	
    35	### Fixed
    36	
    37	General
    38	
    39	- Long-running reconnect and OCSP loops no longer retain unused timers, reducing memory pressure over time (#8204)
    40	- Inherited JWT default permissions are now refreshed when account claims are updated (#8276)
    41	- External auth configuration is now cleared correctly when account claims are updated (#8275)
    42	- PROXY protocol detection, TLS sniffing with `allow_non_tls` and PROXY v1 address-family parsing have been fixed (#8302)
    43	- A race in gateway `CONNECT` handling has been fixed (#8306)
    44	- Trusted proxy tracking no longer leaks closed clients during concurrent updates (#8307)
    45	- Service import replies can now be delivered across cluster routes (#8317)
    46	- Message tracing now works correctly with service imports and exports
    47	- Several panic, fatal and data race conditions in authentication, routing, monitoring and clustered request handling have been fixed
    48	- `NoAuthUser` now checks connection restrictions
    49	- Leaf connections no longer bypass `Nats-Trace-Dest` publish permission checks
    50	- `CONNZ` and `SUBSZ` pagination now guard against `Offset` and `Limit` integer overflow panics
    51	- Fixed a nil pointer panic when starting up when the resolver parent directory is missing (#8329)
    52	
    53	MQTT
    54	
    55	- Partial `CONNECT` packets can no longer exhaust pre-authentication memory
    56	- `PUBLISH` remaining-length underflow no longer causes a server panic
    57	- Subscriptions to internal `$MQTT.deliver.pubrel` subjects are now rejected
    58	- Subscribe deny rules are now enforced on retained message and QoS replay paths
    59	- WebSocket `/mqtt` upgrades no longer panic when MQTT is disabled
    60	
    61	Monitoring
    62	
    63	- JetStream remote usage updates no longer panic on length integer overflow
    64	
    65	JetStream
    66	
    67	- A data race on the cluster meta node during JetStream shutdown has been fixed (#8260)
    68	- Meta proposal inflight tracking is now kept consistent during stream moves and related operations (#8261)
    69	- Stream catchup is no longer skipped when limits are exceeded, preventing possible stream desync (#8265)
    70	- Malformed TTL and schedule state is now rejected during decode (#8269)
    71	- Zero consumer limits are now treated as unlimited during stream updates (#8286)
    72	- Raft nodes no longer participate in voting or candidacy after write errors (#8290)
    73	- Raft checkpoint handling now aborts if the node is closed (#8296)
    74	- Raft `ApplyCommit` now handles the post-snapshot index correctly (#8321)
    75	- Consumer ack subscriptions now match correctly when consumer names contain `%` (#8301)
    76	- Observer state is now cleared correctly during `js_cluster_migrate` when a leaf remote is removed (#8304)
    77	- Atomic batch end-of-batch max-size checks and R1 message rewrites have been fixed (#8305)
    78	- Schedule drift, failed fast batch commits with `gapOk` and stale `/varz` leaf remote state have been fixed (#8308)
    79	- Peer state decoding now bounds peer ID reads to the buffer length (#8310)
    80	- Counter stream staging no longer corrupts the committed running total (#8311)
    81	- Filestore compaction no longer corrupts compressed or encrypted blocks (#8312)
    82	- Memory store `NumPending` no longer overcounts for `DeliverLastPerSubject` consumers (#8313)
    83	- Consumer inactive-delete grace period handling and pull request `MaxBytes` budgeting have been fixed (#8314)
    84	- `MultiLastSeqs` no longer reorders stream config subjects through `filterIsAll` handling (#8315)
    85	- Meta recovery snapshots no longer leave phantom streams or consumers behind (#8324)
    86	- Skipped messages last time no longer violates ordering that could lead to issues with starting by time (#8237)
    87	- Raft now reverts uncommitted membership changes correctly when truncating or snapshotting (#8332)
    88	
