The snapshot shows two gaps in the owner’s read: both workloads use unrestricted `control` credentials, and EVENTS has no byte limit. The 2.14.5 data-loss fix also has a narrower trigger than “offline node catches up”: it involves idempotent stream creation during metalayer snapshot recovery. I’m checking the health probes and rollback limits needed for a concrete rollout.
